  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Anoop Singh vs Pp on 4 July, 2017",
    "facts": "The sample of curd was sent to the Public Analyst who, vide report Exhibit P-13, reported that milk fat content was 5.02%. Milk solids not fat content was 7.86%. Starch and cane sugar were absent. It was opined that the sample does not conform to the prescribed standards under the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules 1955 because it contains about 13% of added water. 5. From the record and specifically the report of the Public Analyst (Exhibit P-13) the position which emerges is that the Food Inspector never claimed to have enquired from the petitioner nor informed the Public Analyst that the curd was made from buffalo milk or cow milk. 6. The defence witnesses have categorically stated that the curd was of Cow's milk.",
